---
/* L30 - cross-entropy: the penalty on a confident mistake is unbounded. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L30.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of two lever balances: on the left a heavy block on a steeply tilted beam with a tall stack of coins beside the pivot, and on the right a level beam holding only a few low coins."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L30-fig-title L30-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L30-fig-title">The penalty for a confident mistake has no ceiling</title>
      <desc id="L30-fig-desc">
        A plot of loss against the probability the model gave the true answer,
        with the horizontal axis on a log scale from 0.001 to 1 and the vertical
        axis from 0 to 7 nats. Two curves are drawn. The cross-entropy curve
        starts near seven nats at probability 0.001, passes two and a third
        nats at 0.1 and just under one nat at 0.5, and falls to almost nothing
        at 1; three labelled points mark 6.908, 2.303 and 0.693 on it. The
        squared-error curve, drawn as a dashed line, stays below one nat
        everywhere on the plot, so the two curves separate sharply on the left.
      </desc>

      <!-- the axes -->
      <g class="fig-axis">
        <path d="M64 300 H616 M64 300 V40" />
      </g>
      <text x="26" y="44" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">6</text>
      <text x="26" y="155" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">4</text>
      <text x="26" y="229" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">2</text>
      <text x="26" y="304" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0</text>
      <text x="56" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0.001</text>
      <text x="234" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0.01</text>
      <text x="420" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0.1</text>
      <text x="550" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0.5</text>
      <text x="592" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">1</text>
      <text x="252" y="336" class="fig-label">probability p, log scale</text>

      <!-- the squared error curve: flat, capped at one nat -->
      <g class="fig-curve fig-curve--weak">
        <path d="M64 263 C 140 263, 300 266, 432 270 C 500 273, 570 290, 616 300" />
      </g>
      <text x="300" y="290" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">(1 - p)^2</text>

      <!-- the cross-entropy curve: no ceiling -->
      <g class="m-draw fig-curve fig-curve--ink" style="--m-length: 700; --m-duration: 2.4s">
        <path d="M64 44 C 90 62, 150 92, 248 129 C 320 165, 380 190, 432 215 C 480 236, 530 260, 560 274 C 585 285, 605 295, 616 300" />
      </g>

      <!-- the labelled points -->
      <g class="fig-point">
        <circle cx="64" cy="44" r="4" />
        <circle cx="432" cy="215" r="4" />
        <circle cx="560" cy="274" r="4" />
      </g>
      <text x="78" y="38" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink">6.908</text>
      <text x="444" y="208" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink">2.303</text>
      <text x="500" y="292" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink">0.693</text>

      <!-- the legend, in the empty upper right -->
      <g>
        <rect x="288" y="50" width="132" height="42" class="fig-panel" />
        <text x="300" y="68" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">-log(p)</text>
        <text x="300" y="84" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">nats, unbounded</text>
      </g>
      <text x="520" y="238" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">at p = 0.9: 0.105</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L30</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Cross-entropy charges nearly seven nats for a confident mistake and has no ceiling, while squared error stays under one nat everywhere on the plot.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text--num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-axis path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-curve path {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-curve--ink path {
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-curve--weak path {
    stroke: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .fig-point circle {
    fill: var(--color-prussian);
  }

  .fig-panel {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule-soft);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
</style>
